I've repped this, it's clearly a bug. The crash and hex dump is 
a dead giveaway. 

It really appears to be two bugs. This only seems to work with 
a tame troll, but not just any tame troll. You have to use the 
necromancer technique Raise Zombies on a troll corpse. The first 
bug is that, instead of a troll mummy, you get a tame troll out 
of this. I'm willing to accept that this bit could be intended 
behavoir, but it is a little wierd.

Next, the troll has to level up until it's willing to attack the
Oracle. Then stroll by. The Oracle will stomp the troll's butt.

Finally, use the technique on the corpse again while it's still 
next to the Oracle. The game crashes, rather spectacularly (at 
least in the ASCII version).

This doesn't seem to affect normal raised undead, nor a tame troll
mummy, nor a normal tame troll, nor your starting ghoul (they'll die
to the Oracle given half a chance but you can raise 'em if there's a 
corpse). It seems to occur only with the Oracle, but I didn't test
that too extensively, because the Oracle is rather unique.

Doctor, it hurts when I do this! 

There's plenty of ways to avoid crashing while still keeping the
troll if you end up in this situation, including hauling the corpse
away before raising it with the technique. So don't do that.

(Incidentally, testing this would be a lot easier with a wizmode
command to reset technique timers. *begs*)

